#drawRoadEdge(ctx, side, color) {
  const N = 58;
  const pxs = Math.max(0.6, this.roadHalf / 418);
  const passes = [
    { mult: 5.2, alpha: 0.085 },
    { mult: 1.7, alpha: 0.85 },
    { mult: 0.55, alpha: 0.95 },
  ];
  for (const pass of passes) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = rgba(color, pass.alpha);
    ctx.lineCap = 'round';
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const z1 = (i / N) * VIEW_DIST;
      const z2 = ((i + 1) / N) * VIEW_DIST;
      const a = this.project(z1, side * 0.995);
      const b = this.project(z2, side * 0.995);
      const avg = (a.s + b.s) / 2;
      ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(0.8, pass.mult * avg * pxs);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(a.x, a.y);
      ctx.lineTo(b.x, b.y);
      ctx.stroke();
    }
  }
  ctx.lineCap = 'butt';
}

drawSpeedLines(ctx) {

Replace with bands 0-45, 45-95, 95-172, N=40 for smoothness. 3 passes × 3 bands = 9 strokes per side. Compute points once. Use the same band mid s. To draw each band path:
```
for pass:
  for band:
    ctx.lineWidth = max(.8, pass.mult*sMid*pxs)
    ctx.beginPath()
    for i 0..N-1:
      const z1=i/N*VIEW_DIST; if (z1<band.lo || z1>=band.hi) continue;
      // need segment to next; if next z > band.hi, clamp? Just include segment starting in band.
      a=project(z1), b=project(z2)
      moveTo lineTo
    stroke
```
At band boundary, segments start at z=band.lo (45 from i/N not exact) and there may be small gaps. With N=40, step 4.3; okay. To avoid gaps, compute points per band with segments split? Simpler use one path per pass for the whole road but constant lineWidth. The perspective thickness variation along the edge is subtle because the edge lines appear mostly thin; could just use constant width per pass (near) and accept constant thickness. But an edge that doesn't taper might look odd near horizon. Use bands with overlaps: include z1 <= band.hi + step. Let's just include seg if z1>=lo-1 and z1<hi and segment end z2 can exceed hi; next band starts around. Minor overlap okay.

Use N=45. Good.

